This project incorporates portions of code from MatGL, specifically derived from:

in "ESF_MEGNet/train":
1- _activations.py: comes from https://github.com/materialyzeai/matgl/blob/v2.0.0/src/matgl/layers/_activations.py. with minor modifications
2- _bond.py: comes from https://github.com/materialyzeai/matgl/blob/v2.0.0/src/matgl/layers/_bond.py
3- _training_dgl.py: comes from https://github.com/materialyzeai/matgl/blob/v2.0.0/src/matgl/utils/_training_dgl.py. with minor modifications and line deletions.
4- layers: comes from https://github.com/materialyzeai/matgl/blob/v2.0.0/src/matgl/layers/_core_dgl.py
and https://github.com/materialyzeai/matgl/blob/v2.0.0/src/matgl/layers/_graph_convolution_dgl.py. We added the 'edge_update_icoxx' function in 'MEGNetGraphConv' along with the changes that comes with such the number of channels, adding a linear layer for the chemicla bonding embeddings, the icoxx embeddings into state and node updates
5- esf_megnet.py: comes from https://github.com/materialyzeai/matgl/blob/v2.0.0/src/matgl/models/_megnet.py. We added transformations to charge, ICOHP, and ICOBI features along with node fusion and ICOHP and ICOBI fusion.


in "ESF_MEGNet/train":
1- dataset.py: comes from https://github.com/materialyzeai/matgl/blob/v2.0.0/src/matgl/graph/_data_dgl.py. We modified it to process charge, ICOHP, and ICOBI.


